>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `exclude_split`

``` hol4
splitLib.exclude_split : string -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Persistently retracts a `[split]` rule.

`exclude_split "Thy.name"` removes the rule `name` of theory `Thy` from
the rules of the `[split]` attribute, in the current theory and its
descendants; `exclude_split "name"` refers to the current theory. The
theorem itself is not deleted. Retracting a name that is not a split rule
has no effect.

To exclude a split rule from a single simplifier call, use
`simpLib.ExclX "split:Thy$name"`.

### Failure

Fails if the `[split]` attribute has not been enabled with
`splitLib.enable_split_attribute`, or if the name is malformed.

### See also

[`splitLib.enable_split_attribute`](#splitLib.enable_split_attribute),
[`simpLib.del_split`](#simpLib.del_split),
[`simpLib.split_ss`](#simpLib.split_ss).
